{
  "case_id": "2022-21-1333",
  "document_hash": "73e33d103042e1deed48435472e9b8c565fc8b64d70d46184f3542e1206bf166",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73e33d103042e1deed48435472e9b8c565fc8b64d70d46184f3542e1206bf166",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73e33d103042-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MALCOLM L. STEWART, Deputy Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting vacatur."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (Eric Schnapper)",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73e33d103042e1deed48435472e9b8c565fc8b64d70d46184f3542e1206bf166",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73e33d103042-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 230(c)(1) distinguishes between claims that seek to hold an internet company liable for content created by someone else and claims based on the company's own conduct. That distinction is drawn in each of the three sections of the statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73e33d103042e1deed48435472e9b8c565fc8b64d70d46184f3542e1206bf166",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73e33d103042-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Snapper -- Schnapper, just so we're clear about what we're -- the -- your claim is, are you saying that YouTube's application of its algorithms is particular to -- in this case, that they're using a different algorithm that --to the one that, say, they're using for cooking videos, or are they using the same algorithm across the board?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73e33d103042e1deed48435472e9b8c565fc8b64d70d46184f3542e1206bf166",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73e33d103042-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: -- an intent, knowledge? There has to be some intent to aid and abet. You have to have knowledge that you're doing this."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1333",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "73e33d103042e1deed48435472e9b8c565fc8b64d70d46184f3542e1206bf166",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73e33d103042-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Those are the facts which led the European Union to fine Google 2.3 billion euros, because they used prioritization to wipe out competition --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73e33d103042e1deed48435472e9b8c565fc8b64d70d46184f3542e1206bf166",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73e33d103042-0003-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position is that the internet service provider can be sued for its own organizational choices, but the fact that it makes organizational choices doesn't deprive it of the protection it receives for liability based on the third-party content."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73e33d103042e1deed48435472e9b8c565fc8b64d70d46184f3542e1206bf166",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73e33d103042-0003-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 81,
        "start": 81
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position is that YouTube's own conduct falls outside of 230(c)(1)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1333",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "73e33d103042e1deed48435472e9b8c565fc8b64d70d46184f3542e1206bf166",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73e33d103042-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 91,
        "start": 91
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: In the government's view, are there any circumstances in which an internet service provider could be sued for defamatory content in a video that it provides?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73e33d103042e1deed48435472e9b8c565fc8b64d70d46184f3542e1206bf166",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73e33d103042-0005-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 109,
        "start": 109
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, for purposes of this case, is there any difference -- let's imagine that the Google algorithm, when you search for ISIS, prioritizes videos produced by ISIS in search results."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73e33d103042e1deed48435472e9b8c565fc8b64d70d46184f3542e1206bf166",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73e33d103042-0005-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 110,
        "start": 110
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Okay. And then what about users and retweets and likes, the question I asked Mr. Schnapper about that. So, you know, I gather 230(c) would protect me from liability if I simply retweeted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73e33d103042e1deed48435472e9b8c565fc8b64d70d46184f3542e1206bf166",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73e33d103042-0005-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 128,
        "start": 128
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But -- but --but what I take you to be saying is that in general -- and this goes back to Justice Thomas's very first question --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73e33d103042e1deed48435472e9b8c565fc8b64d70d46184f3542e1206bf166",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73e33d103042-0007-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 150,
        "start": 150
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Would -- would the -- would Google collapse and the internet be destroyed if YouTube and, therefore, Google were potentially liable for posting and refusing to take down videos that it knows are defamatory and false?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73e33d103042e1deed48435472e9b8c565fc8b64d70d46184f3542e1206bf166",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73e33d103042-0007-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 152,
        "start": 152
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is -- is that right in your view?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Blatt",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73e33d103042e1deed48435472e9b8c565fc8b64d70d46184f3542e1206bf166",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73e33d103042-0007-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 161,
        "start": 161
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If you hold them liable for topic headings, you render the statute a dead letter because you have to organize the content."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "73e33d103042e1deed48435472e9b8c565fc8b64d70d46184f3542e1206bf166",
      "evidence_id": "ev-73e33d103042-0007-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 165,
        "start": 165
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1333",
